course: dictionary
lesson: 1537
title: A word for sea mammals
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names for a whole group of things. Cetacean is one of them. When you meet it, ask: which group of animals is this word naming? «The 'Stute Fish calls the Whale "Noble and generous Cetacean".» The brackets in the story give the clue: a cetacean is a member of the whale and dolphin family, so the fish is calling the whale by the name of its family.
explain: Cetacean is a noun, so you can say a cetacean or some cetaceans. It can also be an adjective, used to describe something that belongs to this group. A dictionary lists both uses, so check which one the sentence needs.
explain: Cetaceans live in the sea, but they are mammals, not fish. They breathe air through a blowhole, they are warm-blooded, and they give birth to live young and feed them milk. Whales, dolphins and porpoises all belong to this group.
fact: Cetacean means any member of the group of sea mammals that includes whales, dolphins and porpoises.
fact: Cetacean is a noun (a cetacean, cetaceans) and can also be an adjective (cetacean).
fact: Cetaceans are mammals: they breathe air, they are warm-blooded, and they feed their young milk.
fact: Some cetaceans, such as baleen whales, filter tiny food through baleen plates, while others, such as dolphins, have teeth.
fact: In «The 'Stute Fish calls the Whale "Noble and generous Cetacean"», the fish uses the formal name for the whale, which is a grand, polite way to speak.
exercise: «The 'Stute Fish calls the Whale "Noble and generous Cetacean".» What is a cetacean? | *A member of the whale and dolphin family | A small wooden boat | A type of seaweed | A kind of fish with fins
exercise: Which of these animals is a cetacean? | A crab | *A dolphin | A shark | A goldfish
exercise: Which fact shows that a cetacean is a mammal and not a fish? | *It feeds its young on milk | It has scales | It lives in a river | It lays eggs in a pond
test: Which word means any sea mammal in the whale and dolphin family? | insect | *cetacean | reptile | fish
test: Which group do porpoises belong to? | Fish | *Cetaceans | Insects | Reptiles
exam: A cetacean breathes air through a blowhole, so it is a | fish | *mammal | reptile | amphibian
